## The problem

`$min-inline-button-size` inside `button-set-fluid-layout()` in [`packages/styles/scss/components/button/_button.scss`](https://github.com/carbon-design-system/carbon/blob/main/packages/styles/scss/components/button/_button.scss) is a **local mixin-scope variable**, making it impossible for consumers to override without forking the mixin. The codebase already acknowledges this limitation in the source comments:

```scss
// May need to be configurable as 3 * 135px is less than 640px.
// Current value 176px only supports up to 3 buttons at 540px.
$min-inline-button-size: convert.to-rem(176px);
```

The value drives all `@container` query breakpoints that control when fluid button sets stack into a column. With `176px` hardcoded:

- **Narrow Tearsheet** (540px wide, 4 buttons): requires a threshold of ≤135px/button to keep buttons inline — 176px causes premature stacking.
- **Side Panel** (lg = 640px, 3 buttons): needs ≤160.33px/button.

IBM Products' Tearsheet component works around this today with a local `$min-inline-button-size: convert.to-rem(120px)` override, but because the variable is mixin-scoped, that override has no effect — the workaround is effectively a placeholder waiting for this upstream fix.

## The solution

Move `$min-inline-button-size` to [`_vars.scss`](https://github.com/carbon-design-system/carbon/blob/main/packages/styles/scss/components/button/_vars.scss) as a public, module-level `!default` variable, following the exact same convention used for every other configurable button property (`$button-height`, `$button-font-weight`, `$button-border-width`, etc.).

**Proposed change to `_vars.scss`:**

```scss
/// Minimum inline size of a fluid button. Used as the container-query threshold
/// for stacking fluid button sets. Contexts with more buttons or narrower
/// containers (e.g. Tearsheet at 540px with 4 buttons) should lower this value
/// via `@use … with ($button-min-inline-size: <value>)`.
/// @type Number
/// @access public
/// @group button
$button-min-inline-size: convert.to-rem(176px) !default;
```

**Proposed change to `_button.scss`** (inside `button-set-fluid-layout()`):

```scss
// Override via `@use '@carbon/styles/scss/components/button' with
//   ($button-min-inline-size: <value>)` for contexts that need a different threshold.
$min-inline-button-size: $button-min-inline-size;
```

This is a **non-breaking change**: the default value remains `176px` (`11rem`), so all existing consumers are unaffected. It unlocks IBM Products (and any other consumer) to configure the threshold at Sass compile time.

> **Note on CSS Custom Properties:** A `var()` approach is not viable here because `@container` query conditions require a resolved `<length>` at parse time — CSS custom properties are not resolved at that stage per the current spec.

## Examples

IBM Products Tearsheet currently carries this dead-override workaround, which this fix makes functional:

```scss
// In tearsheet styles — currently has no effect because the variable is mixin-local
$min-inline-button-size: convert.to-rem(120px);
```

After this fix, IBM Products can use:

```scss
@use '@carbon/styles/scss/components/button' with (
  $button-min-inline-size: convert.to-rem(120px)
);
```

## Design impact

No, the visual default is unchanged.

## Package

`@carbon/styles`

## Project name

IBM Carbon Design System / IBM Products (Carbon for IBM Products — Tearsheet, SidePanel)

## Business priority

Medium Priority — blocks correct fluid button stacking in IBM Products components migrated into Carbon core.
